<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shah Muhammad Sagir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 1400</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shah Muhammad Sagir was a Bengali poet, probably of the reign of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghiyasuddin-azam-shah">Ghiyasuddin Azam Shah</a> around 1400, and one of the earliest known Muslim poets of the Bengali language. His Yusuf-Zulekha retold in Bengali verse the Persian romance of Joseph and Potiphar's wife, opening the long tradition of Bengali romances adapted from Persian literature.</p></div>
